1
00:00:00,030 --> 00:00:00,772
You're a snail,

2
00:00:00,792 --> 00:00:01,160
and you've just

3
00:00:01,180 --> 00:00:01,772
been glued to

4
00:00:01,792 --> 00:00:02,978
a museum card.

5
00:00:02,998 --> 00:00:05,440
London, 1846. Everyone

6
00:00:05,460 --> 00:00:06,320
thinks you're dead.

7
00:00:06,340 --> 00:00:07,157
But you're just sealed

8
00:00:07,177 --> 00:00:07,745
in your shell,

9
00:00:07,765 --> 00:00:08,895
waiting for rain.

10
00:00:08,915 --> 00:00:10,121
Four years pass.

11
00:00:10,141 --> 00:00:11,134
Then someone drops you

12
00:00:11,154 --> 00:00:12,071
in warm water,

13
00:00:12,091 --> 00:00:13,147
and you crawl out.

14
00:00:13,167 --> 00:00:14,409
Your pond-snail cousins

15
00:00:14,429 --> 00:00:15,732
sleep even weirder.

16
00:00:15,752 --> 00:00:16,732
Seven quick naps

17
00:00:16,752 --> 00:00:17,869
in thirteen hours,

18
00:00:17,889 --> 00:00:18,644
then almost two

19
00:00:18,664 --> 00:00:19,879
days wide awake.

20
00:00:19,899 --> 00:00:20,729
Day or night

21
00:00:20,749 --> 00:00:21,631
doesn't matter.

22
00:00:21,651 --> 00:00:22,493
So never trust a

23
00:00:22,513 --> 00:00:24,363
snail that looks dead.
